# See https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

tmp/
e2e.pid
e2e.log
.agents/scratch

# Probably never intentional
*.log
*.txt

# compiled output
dist
out-tsc
__pycache__/

# dispatch-broker/dist is a committed build artifact, not throwaway compiled
# output: action.yml runs it directly (there is no build step at Action-run
# time), so it must be tracked despite the blanket `dist` ignore above. A
# directory match above still hides everything under it from git even with
# a file-level negation, so both the directory and its contents need their
# own negation.
!.github/actions/dispatch-broker/dist
!.github/actions/dispatch-broker/dist/**

# run-dispatch-canary/dist is the same committed-bundle pattern as
# dispatch-broker/dist above (same `build-canary` Nx target, same reason).
!.github/actions/run-dispatch-canary/dist
!.github/actions/run-dispatch-canary/dist/**

# rerun-infra-killed-runs/dist is the same committed-bundle pattern as
# dispatch-broker/dist above (same `build-rerun-infra-killed-runs` Nx
# target, same reason).
!.github/actions/rerun-infra-killed-runs/dist
!.github/actions/rerun-infra-killed-runs/dist/**

# deliverable-watchdog/dist is #721's scheduled observer bundle, built and
# drift-checked by the sibling `build-deliverable-watchdog` Nx target.
!.github/actions/deliverable-watchdog/dist
!.github/actions/deliverable-watchdog/dist/**

# run-webhook-ingress-canary/dist is #796's real GitHub App ingress probe.
# It executes directly from a GitHub-hosted workflow and must be committed,
# rebuilt, and drift-checked like the operational action bundles above.
!.github/actions/run-webhook-ingress-canary/dist
!.github/actions/run-webhook-ingress-canary/dist/**

# dependencies
node_modules
# pnpm falls back to a project-local store here when run inside
